        "reason": "The evidence consistently states the dataset (SESAME) is generated automatically without human labeling. The Abstract says 'we propose a method to automatically generate labeled datasets,' the Introduction says 'construct labeled datasets without human supervision' and 'weakly-supervised... silver standard,' and the Conclusion says 'generate a massively-sized labeled dataset for NER in an automatic fashion, without human labor involved in labeling.' The evidence fully supports answering yes, with the nuance that it is weakly-supervised/silver-standard rather than gold-standard."
